---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// This page explains the editorial access pathways and provides direct access links.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Newsroom Desk — Nick’s Media"
  description="Secure access portal for Nick’s Media editors, journalists, and producers."
  noindex
>
  <article class="legal section-pad" style="max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <div class="section-label">
      <span>Newsroom</span> Editorial Access Portal
    </div>
    <h1>Editorial Workspace &amp; <em>Content Desk.</em></h1>
    <p class="legal-intro">
      Welcome to the Nick’s Media publishing workspace. Our editorial desk is powered by Sanity Studio, where our reporters, editors, and producers draft, review, preview, and publish stories and video content.
    </p>

    <div style="background: var(--navy); color: #fff; padding: 28px; border-radius: 4px; margin: 32px 0;">
      <span style="font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 1.5px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #f6b6b7; font-weight: 700; display: block; margin-bottom: 12px;">DIRECT STUDIO ACCESS</span>
      <h2 style="color: #fff; font-size: 26px; margin: 0 0 12px;">Open Sanity Editorial Studio</h2>
      <p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        Sign in to create, edit, or publish breaking news, articles, and video packages. Use your assigned credentials (Google, GitHub, or Sanity email login) configured for project <code>cgcw2i33</code>.
      </p>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <a
          href="https://manage.sanity.io/projects/cgcw2i33"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="button button-light"
          style="background: var(--red); color: #fff; border-color: var(--red);"
        >
          Open Cloud Studio Desk ↗
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://manage.sanity.io/projects/cgcw2i33/team"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="button button-light"
          style="background: transparent; color: #fff; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3);"
        >
          Manage Editorial Team &amp; Roles ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section style="margin-top: 40px;">
      <h2>How Editorial Authentication Works</h2>
      <p>
        For enterprise production media security, user authentication is managed via Sanity's Role-Based Access Control (RBAC). Passwords are never stored in plaintext or exposed client-side.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Administrator:</strong> Full control over schemas, project settings, API tokens, and user seats.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Editor:</strong> Can draft, review, edit, and publish stories and media directly to production.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Contributor / Author:</strong> Can draft and update stories and submit for editorial review without publishing directly to production.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-top: 36px;">
      <h2>Inviting Team Members (3–4 Logins)</h2>
      <p>
        To grant credentials to your editorial staff:
      </p>
      <ol style="line-height: 1.8; color: #4b5563; font-size: 15px; padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>Go to <strong><a href="https://manage.sanity.io/projects/cgcw2i33/team" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--red); text-decoration: underline;">Sanity Project Team Settings</a></strong>.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>"Invite members"</strong>.</li>
        <li>Enter the editor's email address and assign their role (e.g. <em>Editor</em> or <em>Administrator</em>).</li>
        <li>They will receive a secure single-sign-on invitation email to set their login credentials.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-top: 36px;">
      <h2>Local / Dedicated Studio Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The Studio codebase is also available in this repository under <code>/studio</code>. You can run it locally with:
      </p>
      <pre style="background: #0b192c; color: #f8fafc; padding: 16px; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto; font-size: 13px;"><code>cd studio
npm run dev</code></pre>
      <p style="margin-top: 12px;">
        It opens at <code>http://localhost:3333</code> where team members can log in directly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="legal-actions" style="margin-top: 48px;">
      <a class="button button-dark" href="/">Back to the newsroom ↗</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
